      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "The race revolves around FEAZABEEL (2), who beat MISS STALWART (5) by half a length here in soft going here last time. His mile record is strong and should be full of confidence. MISS STALWART gets a good chance to turn the tables meeting the winner a fraction better at the weights. Travelled well in that same race, owns a win and a placing from three track-and-distance attempts, and had a genuine hold-up two back at Goulburn. SPURLINE (6) is next after a close Goulburn fourth where she was held up near the 200m, with her Forbes fifth also better than her price suggested. All three of her wins have come over the mile and she rates a good chance down in the weights. MIGHTY MYRTLE (1) has weight and the mile is a slight query but the way she's been finishing off suggests she will relish it this time on her home track.",
